
========================================================================
P1  BRAID OS Poincare = prod_{k=1}^{n-1}(1+kt) = Stirling-1st -> tournament cohomology
========================================================================
  n=2: Poincare [1, 1]  == Stirling-1st [c(n,n-i)] [1, 1]? True  (top Betti=1=(n-1)!=1)
  n=3: Poincare [1, 3, 2]  == Stirling-1st [c(n,n-i)] [1, 3, 2]? True  (top Betti=2=(n-1)!=2)
  n=4: Poincare [1, 6, 11, 6]  == Stirling-1st [c(n,n-i)] [1, 6, 11, 6]? True  (top Betti=6=(n-1)!=6)
  n=5: Poincare [1, 10, 35, 50, 24]  == Stirling-1st [c(n,n-i)] [1, 10, 35, 50, 24]? True  (top Betti=24=(n-1)!=24)
  n=6: Poincare [1, 15, 85, 225, 274, 120]  == Stirling-1st [c(n,n-i)] [1, 15, 85, 225, 274, 120]? True  (top Betti=120=(n-1)!=120)
  n=7: Poincare [1, 21, 175, 735, 1624, 1764, 720]  == Stirling-1st [c(n,n-i)] [1, 21, 175, 735, 1624, 1764, 720]? True  (top Betti=720=(n-1)!=720)
  => tournament/ordering space has cohomology pi(t)=prod(1+kt); Betti = Stirling 1st kind.
     A NEW graded lens on the tournament continuum, finer than char_A.

========================================================================
P2  finite-field characteristic polynomial: braid (falling fact) & SHI (deformed braid)
========================================================================
  n=3,q=11: braid #off-all=990==q(q-1)..=990?True | shi #off-all=704==q(q-n)^(n-1)=704?True
  n=3,q=13: braid #off-all=1716==q(q-1)..=1716?True | shi #off-all=1300==q(q-n)^(n-1)=1300?True
  n=4,q=11: braid #off-all=7920==q(q-1)..=7920?True | shi #off-all=3773==q(q-n)^(n-1)=3773?True
  n=4,q=13: braid #off-all=17160==q(q-1)..=17160?True | shi #off-all=9477==q(q-n)^(n-1)=9477?True
  braid regions=n! ; shi regions=(n+1)^(n-1): n=3 -> 6, 16=16 (parking fns).
  => LRC resonances x_i - x_j = integer ARE a deformed braid arrangement; the finite-field
     point-count (Diophantine!) is the native tool -- matching LRC's number-theoretic flavor.

========================================================================
P3  LRC = TORIC arrangement: |G_delta| = complement volume = arithmetic-Mobius (relation lattice)
========================================================================
  v=(1, 2, 3) delta=0.2: |G| direct=0.13333  relation-lattice sum=0.13418  match? True
  v=(1, 2, 3) delta=0.15: |G| direct=0.35000  relation-lattice sum=0.35001  match? True
  v=(1, 3, 5) delta=0.15: |G| direct=0.28667  relation-lattice sum=0.28642  match? True
  => good-set measure = toric-complement volume = arithmetic-Mobius sum over layers {k.v=0}.
     The repo's LRCMod-mod-q ladders (THM-1820) ARE the finite-field method on the torus.

========================================================================
P4  TIGHT = RELATION-RICHEST = max arrangement Mobius/Betti richness: AP (1,2,3) wins
========================================================================
  relation richness N_R (small relations |k|<=2) over primitive n=3 triples, top 6:
     (1, 2, 3): N_R=4   <- the AP / tight extremal
     (2, 3, 4): N_R=3
     (1, 3, 4): N_R=3
     (1, 2, 4): N_R=3
     (4, 5, 9): N_R=2
     (3, 5, 8): N_R=2
  (1,2,3) N_R=4; is it the max? True  (tight = relation-richest = max Betti/Mobius mass)

========================================================================
SUMMARY
========================================================================
  ONE structure -- an arrangement with a Mobius lattice of flats/layers -- recurs across the repo:
   BRAID  (tournaments/NC2, S208): OS cohomology pi=prod(1+kt), Stirling Betti = graded lens.
   SHI/deformed braid (LRC resonance x_i-x_j=integer): finite-field char polynomial (Diophantine).
   TORIC / De Concini-Procesi (LRC relation lattice {k.v=0}, THM-1820): good-set = complement volume
     = arithmetic-Mobius sum = LRCMod mod-q = finite-field method on the torus. Layer-localization is
     the toric analog of the S208 flat-factorization -> a candidate Wall-A tool.
   TIGHT = RELATION-RICHEST: the AP maximizes toric-arrangement Betti/Mobius mass (THM-1820 B2).
  LEVERAGE: (a) tournament cohomology beyond char_A; (b) the finite-field/arithmetic-Mobius method as
  the native engine for LRC characteristic quasi-polynomials; (c) toric layer-localization factoring
  |G_delta| near a resonance, mirroring the braid flat-factorization that gave HYP-8775.
